  "notes": "The debut broadcast of the Internet Elite Wrestling Cup Tournament, airing the first round of its own sixteen-man, single-elimination founding tournament in full (eight matches) live from the Fleet Center in Boston, MA. Between matches, Arthur Essex and valet Robyn Madden cut a promo against IEWC President Dusty Love recalling a short feud the three shared in a prior fed, the ICW; security then ejects Matty Dee, a former Global Wrestling Alliance World Heavyweight Champion, from the arena on Dusty Love's own order after Dee tries to force his way in uninvited.",
