  "notes": "Live from Atlanta, GA. CandyMan opens the show already billed as the undefeated World Heavyweight Champion; \"The Headliner\" Scott Wright defeats an unminted opponent, Sean Slade, in a Featherweight Championship tournament match, and Arthur Essex defeats an unminted opponent, \"Sex Icon\" Jason Gelsomino, in a Television Championship tournament match, both undecided further in this collection's own corpus; Mr. Submission, still carrying a rival promotion's Cruiserweight title belt, submits an unminted ambusher, Bobby Drake. The broadcast's own commentary describes overlapping and inconsistent tournament brackets across the Americas, Television and Featherweight titles this night (at one point naming a Wright-Submission pairing as a final), a continuity slip this collection leaves as broadcast rather than resolving. IEWC President Dusty Love disputes the finish of an Arthur Essex win over him the week before (not in this corpus), announces CandyMan will defend the World Heavyweight Championship against Jack Vars at the promotion's own first supercard, \"November Knockout\" (29 November 1998, MGM Grand, Las Vegas, NV -- a date this collection's own corpus does not reach), and crowns the first Americas Heavyweight Champion.",
